// MT2023 positive-fire: a generic type argument resolves to a value-kind
// def (a function name) rather than a type. Pre-v0.14 this was funnelled
// through MT2002 ("unresolved type"), which mis-described the failure:
// the name DOES resolve, it's just the wrong kind for the position.
// v0.14 (Gap B / MT2023 emit-site) detects the value-name in
// generic-arg position inside `resolve_def_to_ty` and emits MT2023
// directly so users see the kind-mismatch explanation from
// `mty explain MT2023`.
//
// Spec ref: §7.3 (type resolution, kinds) of v1.0-RC2; KNOWN_ISSUES #11
// v1.x emit-landing plan (lifetime kind landing row, refined to
// value-vs-type kind for v0.14 since lifetimes are inferred not
// surface-syntax).
fn helper() -> I32 {
  0
}

fn bad() -> Result[helper, I32] {
  Ok(1)
}
